      "Why instruction and motivation are often the most decisive phase of the hygiene session, and how plaque disclosure and chairside demonstration concretely improve patient adherence over time.",
      "One of the most important — and most often underestimated — phases of a professional oral hygiene session is not the scaling itself, but the following moment dedicated to patient instruction and motivation. What's achieved in the practice, if not maintained with proper technique at home, is undone within days: bacterial biofilm begins reorganizing on cleaned surfaces almost immediately, and it's the quality of daily hygiene, not just recall frequency, that determines the long-term outcome.",
